   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = f(x) \\) be the particular solution to the differential equation \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(1 + y^{2}\\right) \\) with \\( f(1) = \\sqrt{3} \\). The solution exists on a largest open interval \\( (a, b) \\) containing \\( x = 1 \\). Find \\( b \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         1,
         [
            "Divide",
            "Pi",
            3
         ]
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Separate and antidifferentiate: \\( \\arctan y = \\frac{x}{2} + C \\), so \\( y = \\tan(\\frac{x}{2} + C) \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            "x",
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( x = 1 \\): \\( C = \\arctan(\\sqrt{3}) - \\frac{1}{2} = - \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Rational",
               -1,
               2
            ],
            [
               "Divide",
               "Pi",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The tangent is undefined where \\( \\frac{x}{2} + C = \\pm \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\), which gives the neighbours \\( x = 1 - \\frac{5 \\pi}{3} \\) and \\( x = 1 + \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\) of \\( x = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            1,
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     5,
                     "Pi"
                  ],
                  3
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The interval containing \\( x = 1 \\) is \\( \\left(1 - \\frac{5 \\pi}{3}, 1 + \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) \\), so \\( b = 1 + \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
